    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0379" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 339.41/5.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            British Chargé d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 13, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Chargé d’affaires</hi>: I beg to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your personal note of the 17th ultimo, in further
                    relation to the <pb facs="0380" n="264" xml:id="pg264"/> protection of foreign
                    life and property in the Dominican Republic.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to advise you that, on June 24 last, the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marietta</hi> arrived at Sanchez, and that she has
                    instructions to report on conditions in the Dominican Republic, with special
                    reference to the protection of foreign lives and property.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
